      "link_fixes": [
        {
          "original_markdown": "The five configuration properties `adUnitId` (String), `autoReload` (Boolean), `keywords` (String[]), `requestAgent` (String) and `extras` (Object) are readable and writable on both platforms. Changes affect the next load and do not replace an already loaded ad. `autoReload` defaults to `false`; targeting is omitted when unset. Extras retain String, Boolean and numeric primitive values. Internal load/presentation state and native SDK delegate methods are not application APIs.",
          "mirrored_markdown": "The five configuration properties `adUnitId` (String), `autoReload` (Boolean), `keywords` (String[]), `requestAgent` (String) and `extras` (Object) are readable and writable on both platforms. Changes to the four request options affect the next load and do not replace an already loaded ad. `autoReload` defaults to `false` and is read live when the shown ad closes; changing it while an ad is loaded or presented changes whether that close starts a reload. It never automatically presents the replacement or retries a failure. Targeting is omitted when unset. Extras retain String, Boolean and numeric primitive values. Internal load/presentation state and native SDK delegate methods are not application APIs.",
          "reason": "Both native fullscreen dismissal callbacks read the current autoReload property; the four request-targeting options apply on the next load. Verified by the parallel native contract audit; official source unchanged."
        }
